/// Public, static API documentation for the property backend.
///
/// This mixin declares exactly one method, `getApiDoc`, and reads no actor
/// state. The Markdown it returns is authored from the current backend source.
mixin () {
  /// Returns the backend API reference as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Ceylon Property Portfolio Backend API\n\nA single backend canister powers a Sri Lankan real-estate advertising platform. It stores property listings, their photos, visitor enquiries, customer accounts, subscription plans, payments, homepage banners, advertising categories and help-chatbot content. It serves three clearly separate ends: a public property site, a customer account area, and an admin console.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- **Public reads** (`listPublishedListings`, `searchListings`, `getListing`, `listFeaturedListings`, `listPlans`, `getPlan`, `listBanners`, `listCategories`, `listChatbotEntries`) and **enquiry submission** (`submitEnquiry`) are open to anyone, including anonymous callers.\n- **Customer methods** require a signed-in, non-anonymous caller that has registered a customer account. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend and calls `registerCustomer`. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n- **Admin methods** require a signed-in, non-anonymous principal registered in the authorization system with the `admin` role. Customer authentication is entirely separate from admin authentication: a customer account never grants admin access, and an admin principal is not automatically a customer.\n- Non-admin behaviour differs by method shape:\n  - `adminListListings`, `adminListEnquiries`, `adminListCustomers`, `adminListPlans`, `adminListPayments`, `adminListBanners`, `adminListCategories` and `adminListChatbotEntries` return an **empty array**.\n  - `adminGetListing`, `adminGetSubscription` return **`null`**.\n  - Every other admin method returns `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n- Customer methods called by an unregistered or anonymous caller return `#err(#notRegistered)`; customer read methods (`getMyAccount`, `getMyListings`, `getMyListing`, `getMyPayments`, `getMySubscription`) return `null` or an empty array.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- A direct API caller must register through the app's authorization flow before any role-guarded call, guarded queries included.\n\n## Types and units\n\n- `ListingId`, `EnquiryId`, `PlanId`, `PaymentId`, `BannerId`, `CategoryId` and `ChatbotEntryId` are whole numbers (`nat`).\n- `CustomerId` is a `principal`.\n- `Timestamp` is `int`, nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (as returned by `Time.now()`).\n- `Photo` is `{ blob : blob; filename : text }`. `blob` is the platform object-storage reference; `filename` is retained for display and file-type detection.\n- `ListingType` is `#sale` or `#rent`. `PropertyType` is one of `#house`, `#apartment`, `#condo`, `#townhouse`, `#land`, `#commercial`, `#other`.\n- `EmailVerification` is `#unverified`, `#pending` or `#verified`. `MobileVerification` is `#notSubmitted`, `#pendingReview`, `#approved` or `#rejected`.\n- `SubscriptionStatus` is `#active` or `#expired`. `PaymentStatus` is `#pending`, `#confirmed` or `#rejected`.\n- A plan's `listingAllowance` and `imageAllowance` are `?nat`; `null` means unlimited.\n\n## Public site\n\n- `listPublishedListings()` returns every published, unblocked listing, newest first.\n- `searchListings(filter)` filters published, unblocked listings by keyword, listing type, property type, price range, minimum bedrooms and location. All filter fields are optional.\n- `getListing(id)` returns one published, unblocked listing, or `null`.\n- `listFeaturedListings()` returns published, unblocked listings an admin has featured.\n- `submitEnquiry(input)` records an enquiry against a published listing. It returns `#err(#listingNotFound(id))` or `#err(#listingNotPublished(id))` when the listing is missing or unpublished.\n- `listPlans()` returns active plans ordered by `sortOrder`; `getPlan(id)` returns one plan or `null`.\n- `listBanners()` returns enabled homepage banners ordered by `sortOrder`.\n- `listCategories()` returns enabled advertising categories ordered by `sortOrder`.\n- `listChatbotEntries()` returns enabled help-chatbot entries ordered by `sortOrder`.\n\n## Customer account\n\n- `registerCustomer(input)` registers the calling principal as a customer. It returns `#err(#alreadyRegistered)` when the caller already has an account.\n- `getMyAccount()` returns the caller's account with its subscription summary, or `null`.\n- `updateMyProfile(input)` updates name, contact details and advertiser information.\n- `requestEmailVerification(email)` records a verification request for the typed-in address; `confirmEmailVerification(code)` confirms it and returns the updated account. An invalid code returns `#err(#invalidCode)`.\n- `submitMobileNumber(phone)` records a mobile number for admin review. No SMS provider is configured, so the number is never verified automatically; an admin approves or rejects it.\n- `getMyListings()` returns the caller's own listings, newest first. `getMyListing(id)` returns one of them or `null`.\n- `createMyListing(input)` creates a listing owned by the caller. It requires an active subscription and enforces the plan's listing and image allowances, returning `#err(#noActiveSubscription)`, `#err(#listingLimitReached(n))` or `#err(#imageLimitReached(n))`.\n- `updateMyListing(id, patch)`, `deleteMyListing(id)`, `addMyListingPhotos(id, photos)` and `removeMyListingPhoto(id, index)` operate only on listings the caller owns; a listing owned by someone else returns `#err(#notFound(id))`.\n- `submitPayment(planId, reference)` records a payment reference against a plan. The payment starts `#pending` and is **never** marked successful automatically.\n- `getMyPayments()` returns the caller's payment history, newest first. `getMySubscription()` returns the caller's subscription or `null`.\n\n## Subscriptions and payments\n\n- A subscription is created or renewed only when an admin confirms a submitted payment. Confirmation sets the subscription `#active`, records `startedAt`, `expiresAt` (one month later) and `renewedAt`.\n- Subscription status is derived from the expiry timestamp: once `expiresAt` has passed the subscription is `#expired`, and an expired subscription blocks new advertisements until a plan is activated again.\n- Payments are confirmed manually by an admin. There is no automatic payment success path.\n\n## Admin console\n\n- Listings: `adminListListings`, `adminGetListing`, `adminCreateListing`, `adminUpdateListing`, `adminSetListingPublished`, `adminSetListingFeatured`, `adminSetListingBlocked`, `adminDeleteListing`, `adminAddListingPhotos`, `adminRemoveListingPhoto`.\n- Enquiries: `adminListEnquiries`, `adminSetEnquiryRead`, `adminDeleteEnquiry`.\n- Customers: `adminListCustomers`, `adminSetCustomerBlocked`, `adminSetMobileVerification`.\n- Plans: `adminListPlans`, `adminCreatePlan`, `adminUpdatePlan`, `adminDeletePlan`.\n- Payments and subscriptions: `adminListPayments`, `adminConfirmPayment`, `adminRejectPayment`, `adminGetSubscription`.\n- Banners: `adminListBanners`, `adminCreateBanner`, `adminUpdateBanner`, `adminSetBannerEnabled`, `adminReorderBanner`, `adminDeleteBanner`. At most 10 banners may exist; creating an eleventh returns `#err(#bannerLimitReached(10))`.\n- Categories: `adminListCategories`, `adminCreateCategory`, `adminUpdateCategory`, `adminDeleteCategory`.\n- Chatbot: `adminListChatbotEntries`, `adminCreateChatbotEntry`, `adminUpdateChatbotEntry`, `adminDeleteChatbotEntry`.\n- Every admin change controls what appears on the public frontend.\n\n## Structured queries (OQL)\n\n- `schema()` returns a JSON catalogue of the queryable entities: each entity's primary key, fields, field types and edges. It is a `query` call and honours the same per-table authorization as `execute` — entities a caller may not read are omitted, along with edges pointing to them.\n- `execute(qJson)` runs a JSON-encoded read query and returns typed rows. It is a `query` call. A malformed query traps rather than returning an error envelope.\n- Queryable entities and their read authorization:\n  - `listing` (primary key `id`) — public read.\n  - `enquiry` (primary key `id`) — controller/admin only.\n  - `customer` (primary key `principal`) — controller/admin only.\n  - `plan` (primary key `id`) — public read.\n  - `payment` (primary key `id`) — controller/admin only.\n  - `subscription` (primary key `customer`) — controller/admin only.\n  - `banner` (primary key `id`) — public read.\n  - `category` (primary key `id`) — public read.\n  - `chatbotEntry` (primary key `id`) — public read.\n- Variant and collection fields are projected as text or counts: `listingType`, `propertyType`, `emailVerification`, `mobileVerification`, `status` (payment and subscription) render as their tag text; a listing's `photos` array is exposed as the `photoCount` column.\n- OQL is a read-only surface. It never mutates state, so it is safe to retry.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- A newly created listing starts unpublished and unblocked; it appears publicly only after an admin publishes it.\n- A submitted payment stays `#pending` until an admin confirms or rejects it. Poll `getMyPayments()` or `getMySubscription()` to observe the transition.\n- A subscription expires automatically once its `expiresAt` timestamp passes; no call is required to expire it.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `registerCustomer`, `createMyListing`, `submitPayment` and the admin create methods are **not** idempotent: retrying a successful call creates a second record. Check the current state before retrying.\n- `updateMyProfile`, `updateMyListing`, `adminUpdateListing`, `adminUpdatePlan`, `adminUpdateBanner`, `adminUpdateCategory` and `adminUpdateChatbotEntry` are idempotent: applying the same patch twice yields the same result.\n- `adminConfirmPayment` is idempotent in effect: confirming an already-confirmed payment leaves the subscription active.\n- `deleteMyListing`, `adminDeleteListing`, `adminDeleteBanner`, `adminDeleteCategory` and `adminDeleteChatbotEntry` are destructive and remove related records (deleting a listing also deletes its enquiries).\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- `ListingError` is `#notAuthorized`, `#notFound(id)`, `#noActiveSubscription`, `#listingLimitReached(n)` or `#imageLimitReached(n)`.\n- `CustomerError` is `#notAuthorized`, `#notRegistered`, `#alreadyRegistered`, `#invalidCode` or `#notFound(principal)`.\n- `PaymentError` is `#notAuthorized`, `#notRegistered`, `#planNotFound(id)`, `#paymentNotFound(id)`, `#noActiveSubscription`, `#listingLimitReached(n)` or `#imageLimitReached(n)`.\n- `ContentError` is `#notAuthorized`, `#notFound(id)` or `#bannerLimitReached(n)`.\n- `EnquiryError` is `#listingNotFound(id)` or `#listingNotPublished(id)`.\n- `EnquiryAdminError` is `#notAuthorized` or `#notFound(id)`.\n- A plan with `listingAllowance = null` or `imageAllowance = null` is unlimited for that dimension.\n- At most 10 homepage banners may exist at once.\n";
  };
};
